# Settings > Integrations, and the chats' extra environment on the General
# page: what agents start with.

settings-integrations-search-placeholder = Search integrations by name or ID...
settings-integrations-no-window = Open a session window to manage agent integrations. Herdr UI settings remain available.

settings-integrations-chat-env = Chat environment
settings-integrations-chat-env-note = Variables a new chat's tab starts with, here or on an SSH host, such as GH_HOST for GitHub Enterprise or ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL for a company gateway. They are stored in plain text, so keep tokens in your shell or the agent's own sign-in.
settings-integrations-chat-env-invalid = Use NAME=value pairs separated by spaces, with a value in double quotes when it has spaces. HERDR_ACP is set by the app.
settings-integrations-chat-env-apply = Apply environment
